IMPORT prelude

-- Civil Liability Act 1936 (SA), Parts 7A and 7B -- the dates, in one small module. It uses only the built-in date
-- functions (DATE_FROM_DMY, DATE_SERIAL, DATE_FROM_SERIAL), not the daydate library, and defines no YMD.
--
-- Based on content from the South Australian Legislation website, as collected by the Open Australian Legal Corpus on
-- 10 March 2025 (the Act as at 22 June 2023; unofficial, possibly out of date). CC BY 4.0. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for
-- public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Dates for Parts 7A and 7B`

GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the date` d m y MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY d m y

GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE, `the second day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the first day` `is before` `the second day` IF DATE_SERIAL `the first day` LESS THAN DATE_SERIAL `the second day`

GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE, `the second day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days from` `the first day` `to` `the second day` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `the second day` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the first day`

GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE, n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the day` `plus days` n MEANS DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `the day` PLUS n)

-- The days Parts 7A and 7B and s 3A of the Limitation of Actions Act 1936 came into operation, from the legislative
-- histories: Civil Liability (Institutional Child Abuse Liability) Amendment Act 2021 (52/2021) s 4, inserting Parts 7A
-- and 7B, commenced 1.8.2022 (Gazette 28.7.2022 p2373); Limitation of Actions (Child Abuse) Amendment Act 2018
-- (14/2018) s 4, inserting s 3A of that Act, commenced 1.2.2019 (Gazette 22.11.2018 p4010).
`the commencement of Part 7A` MEANS `the date` 1 8 2022

`the commencement of section 3A of the Limitation of Actions Act 1936` MEANS `the date` 1 2 2019
